## Test Smell Audit — Academic 19-Smell Catalog (testsmells.org)

**Target:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` | **Framework:** MSTest 4.1 (.NET 10)  
**Integration calibration:** Applied — class bears `[TestCategory("Integration")]`

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 3           | 3              |
| Medium   | 1           | 1              |
| Low      | 0           | 0              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4**          |

---

### Findings by Severity

#### ❶ Sleepy Test — **High**

**Method:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 87)  
**Integration calibration:** Still High — even integration tests should avoid blind sleeps; async polling or event-wait handles are available.

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000); // ← non-deterministic delay, slows suite
```

**Fix:**
```csharp
var cts = new CancellationTokenSource(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));
while (!_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id))
{
    await Task.Delay(50, cts.Token);
}
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```
**Risk if unfixed:** Flaky CI failures on slow machines; wastes 3 s on every run.

---

#### ❷ Conditional Test Logic — **High**

**Method:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (lines 101–108)

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

One branch never fires — you silently skip assertions, hiding a gap.

**Fix:** Split into two deterministic tests or assert the known type:
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_StandardUser_ReturnsCorrectName()
{
    var user = new User("eve@example.com", "Eve");
    _repository.Insert(user);
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}
```
**Risk if unfixed:** The untested branch rots; bugs hide behind the `if`.

---

#### ❸ Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test) — **High**

**Method:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (lines 113–119)

```csharp
for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
{
    _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
}
// No Assert — passes even if Insert silently no-ops
```

**Fix:**
```csharp
for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));

var users = _repository.ListAll();
Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
```
**Risk if unfixed:** False confidence — coverage shows green but nothing is verified.

---

#### ❹ Assertion Roulette — **Medium**

**Method:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (lines 35–38)

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
// 4 assertions, zero descriptive messages
```

**Fix — add messages:**
```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should persist");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should persist");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Id should be auto-assigned");
```
**Risk if unfixed:** When a failure fires in CI, the developer must read source to identify which property was wrong.

---

### Smell-Free Patterns ✓

The remaining 4 tests (`UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord`, `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase`, `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted`, `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity`) are well-structured:

- Clear Arrange/Act/Assert separation
- Focused on a single behavior each
- Context-obvious count assertions (3 items added → assert 3) — **not** Magic Number
- In-memory SQLite is hermetic — **not** Mystery Guest
- No General Fixture waste (both fields used by all tests)

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Effort | Action |
|----------|-------|--------|--------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | 2 min | Add `Assert.AreEqual(100, ...)` after bulk insert |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | 5 min | Split into two typed tests |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | 10 min | Replace `Thread.Sleep` with polling/timeout loop |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette | 3 min | Add message strings to the 4 assertions |

Fixes 1–2 prevent **false-pass** scenarios and should ship first. Fix 3 reduces flakiness and suite runtime. Fix 4 is ergonomic but lower-risk.
